head - shows first part of a file (10 lines)
head -5 readme.md (show first 5 lines)

Tail - shows last lines of a file

cat (display full content, can also combine files)
Combine files:
cat file1.txt file2.txt file3.txt (shows all content in these files)
Combine + save output in new file:
cat file1.txt file2.txt > newfile.txt

 > - redirect output into a file (overwrite file)

grep(search inside files)

find (find files in directories)
eg. to find all txt files in cd (find . -name "*.txt")
To find all directories/files in home (find /home -type d/find /home -type f)

echo - create file with content using echo
echo bolu > txt1.txt (Creates file and writes “bolu”)

more - view file one screen/page at a time
less -  (better version of more) scroll up/down or search inside file

groupadd (to create group) 

ifconfig (old method) - shows network configuration / IP address
ip (new)
